          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Circle the numbers that are the same— "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ^ { 4 }   \\times   3 ^ { 6 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 ^ { 4 }   \\times   3 ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 ^ { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 ^ { 2 } \\times 6 ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 ^ { 2 4 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.141,
            0.718,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Identify the greater number in each of the following— (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 ^ { 3 }   \\mathrm { o r }   3 ^ { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ^ { 8 }   \\mathrm { o r }   8 ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 0 ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ^ { 1 0 0 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.19,
            0.848,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. A dairy plans to produce 8.5 billion packets of milk in a year. They want a unique ID (identifier) code for each packet. If they choose to use the digits 0–9, how many digits should the code consist of?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.256,
            0.801,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. 64 is a square number (8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ") and a cube number (4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "). Are there other numbers that are both squares and cubes? Is there a way to describe such numbers in general?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.249,
            0.903,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.817,
                0.249,
                0.903,
                0.301
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_26_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.323,
            0.848,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. A digital locker has an alphanumeric (it can have both digits and letters) passcode of length 5. Some example codes are G89P0, 38098, BRJKW, and 003AZ. How many such codes are possible?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.389,
            0.848,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. The worldwide population of sheep (2024) is about 10"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", and that of goats is also about the same. What is the total population of sheep and goats? (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 0 ^ { 9 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 1 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "10^{10}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 1 8 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (v) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times 10^{9}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (vi) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 9 } \\pm 1 0 ^ { 9 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.492,
            0.703,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. Calculate and write the answer in scientific notation:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.549,
            0.984
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
